  "_comment_adr032": "ADR-032: ppi, display_active_mm, panel_module_outline_mm, display_stack_mm, epdc_spi_mhz, refresh timings and reader page geometry are null until E Ink publishes the 10.3\" Kaleido 4 datasheet. Gates skip them loudly; they never fall back to stand-in values.",
  "battery": {
    "chemistry": "Li-ion",
    "charge_limit_v": 4.2,
    "low_alarm_v": 3.4,
    "pack": "replaceable smart pack: cell + protector + pack-side BQ27Z561 gauge, keyed connector (pack+, pack-, SDA, SCL, NTC); no adhesive (ADR-048)",
    "_comment": "ADR-048: one chemistry per hardware revision, no selector. charge_limit_v is the standard Li-ion 4.20 V (AGENTS §4.1 ceiling). low_alarm_v (modelled): the RP2350 raises power-fail here so Linux can flush before the pack protector trips. Firmware refuses to charge a pack whose gauge reports a different design charge voltage."
  },
  "charger": {
    "part": "BQ25798",
    "vreg_min_v": 3.0,
    "vreg_max_v": 18.8,
    "vreg_step_mv": 10,
    "watchdog": "disabled",
    "ship_fet": false,
    "source": "datasheet: TI BQ25798 VREG_RANGE (ADR-035)",
    "_comment_evt0": "datasheet SLUSDV2C. watchdog: expiry returns the charger to default mode and §7.3.2 says VREG returns to the 1s POR value, so it is disabled (REG10 WATCHDOG=0), never fed. ship_fet: VBAT_UVLOZ with a ship FET is 3.25-3.55 V (§6.5), which would block I²C on a deeply discharged pack, so SDRV gets its 1 nF and no FET (ADR-048 keeps this). docs/EVT0_POWER_BOARD.md §3."
  },
